#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""A page on localhost for picking what to cast, instead of typing it.

    cast-ui                serve the page and open it in a browser
    cast-ui --no-open      only serve it
    cast-ui -p 8896        a different port

Casting is already solved: cast-tv relays the stream and the two resolvers turn
a cloud item into an address. This only chooses the material, and then runs the
command a person would otherwise have typed - so whatever was verified against
the TV on the command line behaves the same way here.

The three sources are not alike, and the tabs admit it: GoPro browses over its
API (with a browser token that expires), Google Photos cannot be browsed at all
and starts from a pasted link, and OneDrive is a directory already mirrored to
disk.
"""
